hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1561","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning al-Darawardi, narrated to us, Al-Alaa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah and Sahl, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst ones are The last of them, and the best of the women’s rows are the last, and the worst are the first.”"
"1562","Abu Musa told us, Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told me, Sufyan told us, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best rows for men are the front, the worst are the back, and the best rows for women are “The latter, and the worst of it is the advance. O women, when men prostrate, guard your eyes.” I said to Abdullah: What is that about? He said: Because of the tightness of the waistcoat"
